    "4d1e1f677742618f2efe27bd1ed9dc7f57e12979": {
      "message": "docs(git): correct claims the source contradicts\n\nAn expanded commit shows message, identities, parents and files; the refs\nthe Host returns for it are never rendered, and the row badges cap at\nthree plus \"+N\". The invalid-branch path answers with the Host's own\nsentence (\"… is not a valid branch name\") and keeps git's stderr in\n`cause`, so the README cannot promise git's message on screen. Both\nREADMEs now describe what actually happens.\n\nDocument two things the panel silently does: commit, merge and rebase all\nrun with --no-verify, so the repository's hooks never fire, and\nconflicted rows carry no inline buttons — select them and use the group\nheader instead.\n\ndsh-context7 gains one caveat: renaming `serverName` moves the guidance\nand the tool prefix, but the browser half matches a hardcoded\nmcp__context7__ prefix, so the presentation rows fall back to the default\ntool card.\n\nBump dsh-git to 0.5.1 so the corrected README reaches npm; no runtime\ncode changed. The portal copy follows, and context7 keeps 0.2.1 — its\nonly change here is an omission, not a false statement.",
